Jesus' family lineage
This thing recorded the lineage of Jesus Christ. He is the son of David. And he is the son of Abraham.
Abraham was the father of Isaac. Isaac was the father of Jacob. Jacob was the father of Judah and his brothers.
Yeda was Baba Perez and Zira. Tamar was their mother. Perez was the father of Hazoron. Hazoron was the father of Ram.
Ram was the father of Amminadab. And Amminadab was the father of Nahshon. And Nahshon was the father of Salmon.
Salmon was the father of Boaz. Rahab was the mother of Boaz. Boaz was the father of Obed. Ruth was the mother of Obed. Obed was the father of Jesse.
And Jesse was the father of King David. And David was the father of Solomon. And Solomon's mother was the wife of Uriah.
Solomon was the father of Rehoboam. Rehoboam was the father of Abijah. Abijah was the father of Asa.
He was the father of Jehoshaphat. He was the father of Jehoram. He was the father of Uzziah.
Uzziah is the father of Jotham. Jotham is the father of Ahaz. Ahaz is the father of Hezekiah.
Hezekiah was the father of Manasseh. Manasseh was the father of Amon. Amon was the father of Josiah.
Josiah was the father of Jehoiachin and his brothers. At that time, the Jewish people were forced to leave for Babylon.
After this, the family line continued. Jechoniah was the father of Shallum. Shallum was the father of Zorubbabel.
Zerubbabel was the governor of Abiud. Abiud was the governor of Eliakim. Eliakim was the governor of Azor.
Azur was the father of Zadok. Zadok was the father of Akim. Akim was the father of Eliud.
Eliud was the father of Eliezer, and Eliezer was the father of Mattenai, and Mattenai was the father of Jacob.
Jacob was the father of Joseph. Joseph was the husband of Mary. And Mary gave birth to Jesus, who is called the Christ.
So, there were 14 generations from Abraham to David. And there were 14 from David until the Jewish people had to leave for Babylon. And there were 14 from that time to Christ, the birth of Jesus Christ.
Here is how the birth of Jesus Christ happened. His mother was Mary and Joseph was her betrothed, and they had covenanted to marry. But before they came together, it was revealed to me that she would conceive a child. She was overshadowed by the power of the Holy Spirit.
Her husband, Yusuf, was a righteous man. He did not want to shame her publicly. Therefore, he intended to divorce her secretly.
But while Joseph was thinking about this, an angel of the Lord appeared to him in a dream. The angel said, "Joseph, son of David, do not be afraid to take Mary as your wife. For the child conceived in her is from the Holy Spirit."
She will give birth to a daughter. You must name him Jesus. This is why he will redeem his people from their sins.
All this is happening to bring about what the Lord said would happen. He had said through the prophet,
The virgin is pregnant and will give birth to a son. And his name will be called Emmanuel. (Isaiah 7:14) And the meaning of the name Emmanuel is "God with us".
Joseph got up from sleep. He did what the angel of the Lord commanded him. He took Mary to his house as his wife.
But he did not have relations with her until she gave birth to a son. And he named him Jesus.
The Visit of the Wise Men to Jesus
Jesus was born in Bethlehem of Judea. This took place at a time when Herod was king over Judea. After the birth of Jesus, Magi came from the East to Jerusalem.
They said, "Where is the child who has been born to be the king of the Jews? For we have seen his star in the east and have come to worship him."
King Herod was deeply disturbed when he heard about it. And all the people of Jerusalem were also very troubled.
And Herod secretly called a meeting of the chief priests and teachers of the law. He asked them where the Messiah would be born.
"In Bethlehem of Judea," they replied. "For this is what the prophet has written: 'The voice of one crying out in the wilderness: "Prepare the way of the Lord, make his paths straight."' "
"But you, Bethlehem Ephrathah, though you are small among the clans of Judah, out of you will come for me one who will be a ruler, and he will shepherd my people Israel."
