Jesus left Galilee and went to the region of Tyre and Sidon.
A Canaanite woman who lived near Tyre and Sidon came to him and cried out, "Lord! Son of David! Have mercy on me! My daughter is severely possessed by a demon."
Jesus did not say a single word. His disciples came to him. They begged him, saying, "Send her away, for she keeps crying out after us."
Jesus answered, "I was sent only to the lost sheep of Israel. They are like a flock of sheep that has wandered off, every one going its own way."
And then the woman knelt before him. "Oh Lord! Help me!" she said.
Answer, "It is not right to take the children's bread and give it to the dogs."
"Yes, sir," she said. "But even dogs eat the crumbs that fall from the table of their masters."
And Jesus answered and said, "Woman, great is your faith! Let it be done for you as you desire." And her daughter was healed at that very moment. Jesus feeds four thousand people.
Jesus left there. He went beside the Sea of Galilee. Then he went up on a mountain and sat down.
Large groups of people brought him. They brought the blind and those who could not walk. They even brought those who were crippled, those who could not speak, and many others. They placed them at his feet, and he healed them.
The people were amazed. Those who could not speak were speaking. The disabled saw healing. Those who could not walk were walking. The blind saw. And so the people praised the God of Israel.
From afar Jesus called His disciples to come to Him. He said, "My heart is deeply touched by these people. They have been with Me for three days and have nothing to eat. I do not want to send them away hungry. If I did, they would collapse on the road due to weakness."
His disciples answered him. They said to him, "There is nothing here," they said. "Where would we get enough bread to satisfy these many people?"
